      "rationale": "The report says a regression makes basic sqlparse operations raise TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'NoneType' and 'int', naming 'valid args', 'cli multiple files with inplace', and normal-SQL DoS-prevention checks as failing among 41 total. Since the crashing code path (StatementSplitter, used by parse/format/split and hence by the CLI and formatter.validate_options pipeline) underlies virtually every public entry point, I wrote three tests that each exercise one of the named failing behaviours through the library's own documented API: validate_options + format with ordinary valid options, the sqlformat CLI's documented --in-place/multi-file support, and plain parse()/format() of an everyday SELECT statement. Expected values (option values passed through unchanged, exit code 0 with files rewritten to contain 'SELECT', statement type 'SELECT', keywords upper-cased) come directly from the functions' docstrings/CLI help text and obvious intended behavior, not from any current buggy output, so the tests fail while the regression is present and pass once statement splitting/DoS-prevention is fixed correctly.",
